From: Duy Truong <duytruong@google.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 16:06:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix stack-buffer-overflow in StagefrightMetadataRetriever

StagefrightMetadataRetriever::parseMetaData() used sprintf with %f to format a float into a 32-byte buffer. An attacker-supplied float (e.g., FLT_MAX) could result in an output of up to 47 bytes, causing a stack buffer overflow.

This change replaces sprintf with snprintf in StagefrightMetadataRetriever.

Bug: 503551664
Test: manual repro with PoC
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX

Note: This was autogenerated by MendIt (go/androidmendit)
Cherrypick-From: https://googleplex-android-review.googlesource.com/q/commit:8407b6db81e0ba453f9aaeea9557a6596c6077a1
Merged-In: I5a9b333b7c0f14e5a4ebfb31f3fd3dbbe7e5f6aa
Change-Id: I5a9b333b7c0f14e5a4ebfb31f3fd3dbbe7e5f6aa
---
 media/libmediaplayerservice/StagefrightMetadataRetriever.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/media/libmediaplayerservice/StagefrightMetadataRetriever.cpp b/media/libmediaplayerservice/StagefrightMetadataRetriever.cpp
index 86791419db..03332d85e9 100644
--- a/media/libmediaplayerservice/StagefrightMetadataRetriever.cpp
+++ b/media/libmediaplayerservice/StagefrightMetadataRetriever.cpp
@@ -614,7 +614,7 @@ void StagefrightMetadataRetriever::parseMetaData() {
 
     float captureFps;
     if (meta->findFloat(kKeyCaptureFramerate, &captureFps)) {
-        sprintf(tmp, "%f", captureFps);
+        snprintf(tmp, sizeof(tmp), "%f", captureFps);
         mMetaData.add(METADATA_KEY_CAPTURE_FRAMERATE, String8(tmp));
     }
 
